			<div class="content" id="post-content-4747473">
									

<p>Hello all, long time lurker and decided it is finally time to make the plunge. I really felt I wanted to be able to show appreciation for how this community has helped me, even if no one ever knew it previously but me.</p>
<p>I first learned about the SCP, and this community, after a convoluted ride that started with Junji Ito and ended up with a reddit discussion where someone mentioned some of the SCPs. This was in mid 2017 and I casually started reading the site at that time.</p>
<p>In December of 2017 I was in a horrendous accident involving being rear ended by a semi. After this a lot of things changed, the SCP wiki became a lifeline for me and was instrumental in retraining my brain. It has really helped me rebuild a lot of my problem solving, deductive, and reasoning skills as well as my ability to quickly grasp the whole picture being laid out.</p>
<p>Clef, djkaktus, Kalinin, CadaverCommander, Djoric, &amp; Ihp have written or been in involved in some of my favorite SCPs, Tales, and GoIs though that list is by no means exhaustive.</p>
<p>I'm going long and don't want to write a novel but I'm glad to be here and hope to contribute soon. I mainly like to relax by either reading novels, watching anime, or gaming (console, PC, board games, I'm equal oppurtunity).</p>

