<p>Hello there, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/torumsie" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6729404); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6729404&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1597610851" alt="TorumSie" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6729404)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/torumsie" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6729404); return false;">TorumSie</a></span>. Welcome to the SCP Wiki!</p>
<p>Great to see that after reading around, you've created a Wikidot account to interact more with the on-site community. I've noticed quite a few people have found out about the site via reddit, and it's really cool to see how it's a big enough topic for a good number of people to have gotten into SCP with the platform.</p>
<p>I'm so sorry to hear about your accident, but I'm at least glad the wiki was able to help you power through it in some way. If you're interested in djkaktus' work, I suggest you check out their latest article <a href="/scp-5935">SCP-5935</a>. Anyway, here are some resources that should help you navigate the site:</p>
<h3><span>Navigation:</span></h3>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>If you want to keep up with the latest material, check out the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/most-recently-created">Most Recently Created</a> page. If you'd rather check out only the most popular new articles, then <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/top-rated-pages-this-month">Top Rated New Pages</a> is the way to go.</p>
<p>While you're browsing, if you find an article you absolutely love, you can try finding more from the same author by looking them up on the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/members-pages">Authors' Page</a> hub. If the user in question is not on that list, you can try searching for them on our statistic site, <a href="http://scpper.com">scpper.com</a>.</p>
<p>If there are some SCPs that you're a fan of, you can try checking out a new addition to the wiki: the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-series-1-tales-edition">SCP Series Tales List</a>, created by yours truly. These are pages that mirror the main SCP listings, but they include all the stories that feature each SCP (for example, one can find everything that has been written about SCP-173).</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<h3><span>Recommendations:</span></h3>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>With the amount of SCPs we have, it can be hard to find <em>really</em> good articles in specific genres (not to mention we have no way of searching by genre), so I took it upon myself to curate a few lists of some good representative material to share with other users. With the help of various community members, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/user-curated-lists">User-Curated Lists</a> has been built to facilitate fun wikiwalks of some amazing content!</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Anyways, this should be more than enough to get you started! Let me know if this message was helpful at all, and if there's anything important you think I may have missed. Happy reading!!</p>

